## Creating child issues (expanded bodies)

Every child issue in this workflow gets an **expanded body**: the complete instructions for its step, so coder and reviewer bots never need to open a skill. Each body is in the step's section below, inside a 4-backtick `markdown` fence between two marker comments, `child-body:<step-id>:start` and `child-body:<step-id>:end`. The step ids are `step-1a`, `step-1b`, `step-2`, `step-3` and `step-4`.

When a step tells you to open a child issue:

1. **Never write, summarize, shorten or reorder the body yourself.** It must be the exact block for that step, with only these placeholders replaced:
   - `{kind}` → the Kind from the parent issue title (`ai:feat: KCC support for <Kind>`), e.g. `DialogflowWebhook`
   - `{kind_lowercase}` → the same Kind in lowercase, e.g. `dialogflowwebhook`
   - `{parent_issue}` → the parent workflow issue number (`${SESSION_ID#issue-}`)

   Leave every `<angle-bracket>` placeholder as it is; the coder fills those in.
2. **Extract the body** with this script. Set `KIND` and `STEP`:
   ```bash
   PARENT="${SESSION_ID#issue-}"
   KIND="<Kind>"
   STEP="<step-id>"
   KIND_LOWER="$(printf '%s' "${KIND}" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')"
   WF_URL="$(gh issue view "${PARENT}" --repo GoogleCloudPlatform/k8s-config-connector --json body --jq .body \
     | grep -oE 'https://raw\.githubusercontent\.com/[^[:space:])]+' | head -n 1)"
   WF_URL="${WF_URL:-https://raw.githubusercontent.com/acpana/k8s-config-connector/refs/heads/acpana-bulkgen-wf/.agents/workflows/kcc-greenfield-bulkgen}"
   BODY_FILE="$(mktemp)"
   curl -fsSL "${WF_URL}" | tr -d '\r' \
     | awk -v s="${STEP}" '$0 == "<!-- child-body:" s ":start -->" {f=1; next} $0 == "<!-- child-body:" s ":end -->" {f=0} f' \
     | sed '1d;$d' \
     | sed -e "s/{kind_lowercase}/${KIND_LOWER}/g" -e "s/{kind}/${KIND}/g" -e "s/{parent_issue}/${PARENT}/g" \
     > "${BODY_FILE}"
   head -n 1 "${BODY_FILE}" | grep -qx "<!-- kcc-greenfield-bulkgen:${STEP} -->" \
     && tail -n 1 "${BODY_FILE}" | grep -qx "<!-- end kcc-greenfield-bulkgen:${STEP} -->" \
     && ! grep -qE '\{(kind|kind_lowercase|parent_issue)\}' "${BODY_FILE}" \
     && echo "body OK ($(wc -c < "${BODY_FILE}") bytes)"
   ```
   If `curl` isn't available, copy the step's block from this workflow into `${BODY_FILE}` verbatim (only the placeholder substitutions above), then run the same three checks.
3. **Create the issue** with `--body-file`, never `--body`, using the title and labels from the step and the parent's assignees:
   ```bash
   gh issue create --repo GoogleCloudPlatform/k8s-config-connector \
     --title "<title from the step>" \
     --label "<labels from the step, comma-separated>" \
     --assignee "<parent-assignees-comma-separated>" \
     --body-file "${BODY_FILE}"
   ```
4. **If the checks in 2 fail**, don't create the issue. Post one short comment on the parent issue saying that body extraction failed for `<step-id>`, and stop. Never fall back to a body you wrote yourself.
5. **Adopted issues.** If you adopt an existing child issue (see the guardrails above) whose body doesn't contain `kcc-greenfield-bulkgen:<step-id>`, and it has no linked PR yet, replace its body with the extracted one: `gh issue edit <issue-number> --repo GoogleCloudPlatform/k8s-config-connector --body-file "${BODY_FILE}"`.
6. **Keep the workflow link.** If you edit the parent issue description, always keep its `Workflow: <url>` line.

## Steps

Each step says when to open its child issue, gives the title, assignees and labels, and holds the expanded body.

### Step 1a: Prepopulate Direct API Types, Identity, and Judgement Queue

Check whether `{kind}` has already been prepopulated on `master` (i.e., `apis/<service>/v1alpha1/{kind_lowercase}_types.go` exists on `master`, or `apis/<service>/judgement_queue.yaml` on `master` already contains `kind: {kind}`):
*   If `{kind}` is **already** prepopulated in `apis/<service>/judgement_queue.yaml` on `master`, mark **Step 1a** as `Completed (Bulk Prepopulated)` in the progress table and proceed immediately to **Step 1b**.
*   If `{kind}` is **not** yet on `master`, open a GitHub issue to prepopulate the initial KRM types, identity, and `judgement_queue.yaml` for `{kind}` using `--prepopulate-resource`.

**GitHub Issue Details for Step 1a (Prepopulate):**
*   **Title:** `Greenfield: Prepopulate direct KRM types, identity, and judgement queue for {kind}`
*   **Assignee:** Inherit assignees from the parent workflow issue (`${SESSION_ID#issue-}`)
*   **Labels:** `overseer`, `greenfield`, `step/gen-types`, `overseer/review`
*   **Body:** extract `step-1a` (see "Creating child issues"). It is this block:

