**Parent workflow:** #{parent_issue} | **Kind:** `{kind}` | **Step 1a: Prepopulate** (pipeline: **1a** → 1b → 2 → 3 → 4)

> [!NOTE]
> This issue is self-contained: it inlines every KCC skill this step needs, so you don't need to open anything under `.gemini/skills/`. If a skill, a doc under `docs/`, or `GEMINI.md` disagrees with this issue, follow this issue.

Step 1a scaffolds `{kind}` mechanically with `controllerbuilder`: KRM types, identity, reference, mapper and CRD. The generator also writes `apis/<group>/judgement_queue.yaml`, the list of decisions it couldn't make. **You make none of those decisions here**; Step 1b triages the queue.

## Values you need

| Value | Meaning | How to find it |
|---|---|---|
| `<group>` | Group prefix. Types live in `apis/<group>/v1alpha1/`, the API group is `<group>.cnrm.cloud.google.com`, controllers live in `pkg/controller/direct/<group>/`. | If `apis/<group>/` already has kinds with the same prefix as `{kind}`, reuse it. Otherwise use the lowercase service name from the proto package (`google.cloud.apihub.v1` → `apihub`). |
| `<proto.package>` | Proto package, e.g. `google.cloud.apihub.v1`. | Section 1. |
| `<ProtoMessage>` | Proto message of the resource, e.g. `Plugin`. | Usually `{kind}` without the group prefix. Confirm with `grep -i <name> docs/ai/metadata/cloudassetinventory_names.jsonl` and the proto. |
| `<service_name>` | Short GCP service name, as in `<service_name>.googleapis.com`. Used for the journal. | The proto's `option (google.api.default_host)`. |

## Guardrails

- **Already done?** Run `git fetch origin master && git grep -n "kind: {kind}$" origin/master -- 'apis/*/judgement_queue.yaml'`. A hit means `{kind}` was bulk-prepopulated: don't open a PR, comment that on this issue, and stop.
- **No hand edits** to `{kind_lowercase}_types.go`, `types.generated.go`, `{kind_lowercase}_identity.generated.go`, `{kind_lowercase}_reference.generated.go` or `apis/<group>/judgement_queue.yaml`. (Section 4.3 has the one exception.)
- **Resolve no queue entries.** `untriaged-bulk-generation` for `{kind}` must stay `status: open`.
- **No `--allow-non-ga-proto`.** If the resource only exists in a non-GA proto (`v1alpha*`, `v1beta*`), stop and comment on this issue.
- **Stay in scope.** Touch only `{kind}`'s files and the shared files named below. Don't refactor other resources.
- **Don't edit any `SKILL.md`.** Put general learnings in the PR's "Workflow feedback" section.

## 1. Find the proto (GA only)

1. If `.build/third_party/googleapis` is missing, run `./dev/tools/controllerbuilder/generate-proto.sh`.
2. Find the message: `grep -rn "^message <ProtoMessage> {" .build/third_party/googleapis/google/`.
3. Confirm the package is GA (`v1`, `v2`, `v4`, …). Note its `option (google.api.resource)` pattern(s) and `Create<ProtoMessage>Request`.

## 2. Configure `apis/<group>/generate.sh`

If the group is new, create the script; otherwise add `{kind}` to it. All three `controllerbuilder` commands get `--prepopulate-resource`:

```bash
#!/bin/bash
# Copyright 2026 Google LLC
#
# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License");
# you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.
# You may obtain a copy of the License at
#
#      http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
#
# Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software
# distributed under the License is distributed on an "AS IS" BASIS,
# WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.
# See the License for the specific language governing permissions and
# limitations under the License.

set -o errexit
set -o nounset
set -o pipefail

REPO_ROOT="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"

CONTROLLERBUILDER="${CONTROLLERBUILDER:-}"
if [[ -z "${CONTROLLERBUILDER}" ]]; then
  if [[ -x "${REPO_ROOT}/bin/controllerbuilder" ]]; then
    CONTROLLERBUILDER="${REPO_ROOT}/bin/controllerbuilder"
  else
    CONTROLLERBUILDER="go run ${REPO_ROOT}/dev/tools/controllerbuilder"
  fi
fi
source "${REPO_ROOT}/dev/tools/goimports.sh"
cd ${REPO_ROOT}/dev/tools/controllerbuilder
./generate-proto.sh

${CONTROLLERBUILDER} generate-types \
  --service <proto.package> \
  --api-version <group>.cnrm.cloud.google.com/v1alpha1 \
  --include-skipped-output \
  --resource {kind}:<ProtoMessage> \
  --prepopulate-resource

${CONTROLLERBUILDER} generate-identity \
  --service <proto.package> \
  --api-version <group>.cnrm.cloud.google.com/v1alpha1 \
  --resource {kind}:<ProtoMessage>

${CONTROLLERBUILDER} generate-mapper \
  --service <proto.package> \
  --api-version <group>.cnrm.cloud.google.com/v1alpha1 \
  --include-skipped-output \
  --prepopulate-resource

cd ${REPO_ROOT}
dev/tasks/generate-crds

if [ -d "${REPO_ROOT}/pkg/controller/direct/<group>" ]; then
  go run -mod=readonly golang.org/x/tools/cmd/goimports@${GOLANG_X_TOOLS_VERSION} -w pkg/controller/direct/<group>/
fi
```

- **Order.** Every `generate-types` and `generate-identity` call comes before `generate-mapper`, followed by `cd ${REPO_ROOT}`, `dev/tasks/generate-crds` and `goimports`. In an existing script, insert the new blocks **above** `generate-mapper`, never below it; otherwise the mapper is generated before `types.generated.go` is updated.
- **Groups with `v1beta1` kinds.** Pass `--multiversion` and `--prepopulate-resource` to the single `generate-mapper` call, targeting `<group>.cnrm.cloud.google.com/v1beta1`.
- `--prepopulate-resource` already turns on the bulk-generation options (`--emit-plural-acronyms`, `--emit-message-maps`) in `generate-types` and `generate-mapper`. Don't add them yourself.

## 3. Generate, block the kind from releases, and compile

1. Run the script:
   ```bash
   chmod +x apis/<group>/generate.sh
   ./apis/<group>/generate.sh
   ```
2. **`BLOCKED_KINDS`.** Add `{kind}` to the `BLOCKED_KINDS=( ... )` array in `dev/tasks/build-release-bundle`: 4-space indent, double quotes (`    "{kind}"`), alphabetical order, no duplicates. This keeps the unverified CRD out of the release bundle (`operator/channels/packages/configconnector/*/crds.yaml`) until a graduation step removes it at the end of the pipeline.
3. **New API group?** If `dev/tasks/generate-crds` added the group to `config/installbundle/components/clusterroles/cnrm_admin.yaml` or `cnrm_viewer.yaml`, keep the operator files in sync:
   ```bash
   ./dev/tasks/generate-channels
   WRITE_GOLDEN_OUTPUT=1 go test ./operator/pkg/controllers/configconnector/...
   ```
4. Check that `apis/<group>/judgement_queue.yaml` exists and has `reason: untriaged-bulk-generation` with `status: open` for `{kind}`.
5. Compile:
   ```bash
